High School Management System

1. Introduction to Testing
Software testing is the process of evaluating a software system to identify defects, bugs, errors, or unexpected behavior. It helps developers check whether the system works correctly and whether it meets the expected requirements.

Testing is important in software development because it improves:
reliability
correctness
security
maintainability
user experience

For this project, testing was important because the High School Management System includes sensitive school data such as users, grades, attendance records, schedules, document requests, and notifications. If these features do not work correctly, students, teachers, or IT staff may receive wrong information or be unable to perform their tasks.

2. Purpose of Testing
The purpose of testing this system was to make sure the most important parts of the application work correctly under different conditions.

Testing helped us verify that:
users can log in with valid credentials
users cannot log in with invalid credentials
role-based access works correctly
IT staff can create, update, and delete schedules
teachers can create, update, and delete announcements
invalid or incomplete inputs are rejected
the system returns proper success and error messages

Testing also helps identify defects early so they can be fixed before the final project presentation.

3. Selected Components for Testing

For this project, three important components were selected for testing:
1. Login Function
2. Schedule Management
3. Announcement Management

These components were selected because they are critical to the functionality and security of the system.

Component 1: Login Function
Why this component is important
The login function is one of the most important parts of the system because it controls access to the application.

If the login function does not work correctly:
valid users may not be able to access the system
unauthorized users may gain access
users may be sent to the wrong dashboard
role-based security may fail

The login function checks:
whether email and password are provided
whether the user exists
whether the password is correct
whether the account is active
which role the user has

The system has three roles:
Student
Teacher
IT Staff

After login, each user is redirected to the correct dashboard.

