9. Reflection

Testing showed that the High School Management System works correctly for the selected critical components. The login function is secure enough for the project because it verifies credentials, checks account status, and assigns user roles. Schedule management works correctly for IT staff and prevents unauthorized users from creating schedules. Announcement management works correctly for teachers and students, while preventing students from accessing teacher-only actions.
The tests also showed the importance of role-based access control. Since the system has different users with different permissions, testing access restrictions is very important.

